  "reroute_reason": {
   "kind": "rtl_change",
   "reason": "KV-GRP2 structural redesign (owner: one failed route = redesign): sq1 clock FAIL 114/124 ps and the sq2/sq3 gates retired on source prerequisites (y__tep alias hold -74.9 ps, unregistered i_ctl cones, 9.98 contacts/um SRAM faces, 8-deep LD shift chain).  New RTL qkd_kvs_grp_s2 (registered faces, landed resets, p192 rows 5.09/um, LD ring, Stage 1 private ABI, DOMSPLIT o_pc 33+95), new pins, new macros. KV-GRP3 (s2 gate review): every s2 variant FAILED textbook.reset_landing (rst_n reached 13 flops, hrst_n 8: the per-leaf copies were cleared by the port) and grp_s2c had reg->out -133 ps on o_ctl[32] (i_up landed at the S face drove the N-face pin across the tile in one cycle).  s3: the port clears only the first landing stage (copies cleared by the landed stage, D = 1, same release edge), o_ctl / o_dn leave exit face flops (+1 core edge each, priced, KV-GEN9 inbox). KV-GRP6 s6 (Codex s5 storage audit c1e5bec49): the 1024-b response payload passed four unchanged flop captures (PC out e0 -> hop e1 -> idata e2 -> exit e3; the middle three a >= 3-deep delay line, SAFE 5).  s6: per PC branch the payload delay is a genuine SRAM ring (8 x 4x32 1R1W macros, write slot wp at e1, read the previous slot at e2, exit copies at e3; unreset self-phasing pointers, read != write slot), payload cleared exactly as the old hop cleared it; metadata keeps its hop; two kept exit copies on both tiles; +0 cycles."
  },
  "views_to": "physical/ref_tile/qkd_kvs_grp_h_s6ra/views",
  "record_to": "results/rtl/ref_tile/qkd_kvs_grp_h_s6ra"
 },
 "pin_regs": {
  "enable": false,
  "reason": "The RTL registers every face (tools/qwen_kv_die/kv_grp_safe2.py): i_ctl / i_up / x__est land on kept face flops (one copy per consumer leaf), PC / K / V inputs land on the landing / row-control input flops, every output leaves a flop (no combinational input->output path); the ages are bench-proven against the unchanged tile (kvs_grp_s2_bench.py) and handed to the die schedule.  A flow-inserted pin stage would add an unpriced cycle."
 },
